course: dictionary
lesson: 280
title: Making amends
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words are almost always used in one special phrase. Amends is one of them: you hardly ever meet it on its own. You meet it in «make amends», and the words around it tell you what it means. «Making amends can be done with work, such as painting, cleaning or helping, not only with words.»
explain: Look at the clues. Making amends is something you do, not just something you say, and it comes after a wrong. «Saying sorry starts putting things right; making amends finishes it, by fixing, replacing or paying back what you damaged.» So amends is the action that puts a wrong right.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. Swap in "doing something to put the wrong right" and check: «Bullies often do not see how much they hurt someone; seeing it clearly can change them, and making amends helps.» It still makes sense, so you have found the meaning.
fact: Amends means something you do to show you are sorry and to put right a wrong you did.
fact: Amends is nearly always used in the phrase "make amends", so learn the phrase as one chunk.
fact: «Making amends» can mean fixing, replacing or paying back what you broke or damaged.
fact: Saying sorry is a start, but making amends goes further, because it is an action that puts things right.
fact: You can make amends for something, as in «make amends for breaking a friend's toy», or make amends to someone.
exercise: «Making amends can be done with work, such as painting, cleaning or helping.» What does making amends mean? | Winning a game against a friend | Writing a long story about a wrong | Forgetting about a wrong you did | *Doing something to put a wrong right
exercise: Tom breaks his sister's model plane. Which one is making amends? | He hides the broken pieces under the bed | He tells his friend it was not his fault | He buys a new game for himself | *He glues the plane back together and says sorry
exercise: Ella wants to make amends for losing Sam's book. What should she do? | Keep the book and hope Sam forgets | *Find or replace the book, or pay for it, and say sorry | Tell Sam the book was never important | Lend Sam a pen
test: Which of these is a way of making amends? | *Paying back the money for a window you broke | Saying nothing and walking off | Shouting at the person you hurt | Blaming someone else
test: «Bullies often do not see how much they hurt someone; seeing it clearly can change them, and making amends helps.» Why does this matter? | Making amends is only for adults | Bullies never need to say sorry | *Seeing the hurt clearly can lead them to make amends | It shows bullies are happy
exam: In «make amends for breaking a friend's toy», what does amends mean? | A loud shout to show anger | A toy you buy to keep | A game you play with a friend | *Something you do to show you are sorry and put a wrong right
